Following a detailed investigation of the Microsoft Sentinel alerts, it was confirmed that no unauthorized access was successfully achieved 
through the observed RDP brute-force activity. All authentication attempts resulted in failed logon events, and the virtual machine remained uncompromised 
throughout the duration of the attack.

To further strengthen the security posture of the environment, several defensive improvements are recommended. 
These include implementing network-level firewall controls for the virtual network and enabling Microsoft Defender for Cloud 
to provide enhanced threat protection and continuous security monitoring.

As an additional hardening measure, Just-In-Time (JIT) virtual machine access through Microsoft Defender for Cloud. 
JIT access would restrict inbound RDP traffic by default and allow access only when explicitly requested and approved, 
significantly reducing the attack surface and mitigating future brute-force attempts.


